        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The Elite 100 V2 is the best Bluetti power station for most people. It hits the sweet spot of capacity, output, weight and solar input, and its 4,000-cycle battery will outlast most of the devices you plug into it. If you are on a tight budget and charge mostly from the wall, a discounted AC180 delivers similar everyday performance for less.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Step up to the AC200L if you want a system that can grow from 2 kWh to 8 kWh, and to the Apex 300 if your real goal is backing up house circuits, including 240V loads. For camping and CPAP backup, the Elite 30 V2 and EB3A are the right size. Whatever you choose, size it to your actual loads, match your panels to its solar input and never connect it to your house without a proper transfer switch.
          </p>
